# chrony FHS migration: runtime dir pinned to /var/run/chrony.
#
# History that matters: the recipe previously passed
# --runstatedir=/run, which chrony's custom configure does not
# recognise (it parses --chronyrundir/--chronysockdir only), so the
# flag was silently ignored and every published build used the
# upstream default /var/run/chrony. Live /var/run/chrony paths were
# therefore always genuine - never symlink artifacts. The recipe now
# passes --chronyrundir=/var/run/chrony explicitly, so the path is
# intentional rather than accidental. No old residue exists to
# migrate; this fragment converges ownership and guards the path.
#
# Stale-state policy (/var/run is persistent by design, never wiped):
# fully daemon-side, verified in chrony-4.8 source (main.c
# check_pidfile: live pid refuses start, dead pid overwritten;
# socket.c bind_unix_address: unlinks before bind). Service files
# only ensure the directory - no pid/socket cleanup anywhere.
#
# Mode is 0700 root:root, not 0755: chrony.conf(5) requires the
# command-socket directory be accessible only to trusted users and
# disables the socket on world access. This service runs as root
# (-u root), so root-only is the correct arrangement (0750
# chrony:chrony would be the alternative for an unprivileged user -
# a separate improvement, not this fix).

dir /var/run/chrony 0700 root root
